WEBVTT

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.030
<i>Let me introduce you to your manager.</i>

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.610
I'm Takanashi Tsumugi.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.030
I'm glad to be working with you.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.160
I'm Izumi Iori.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.530
I'm Nikaido Yamato.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.870
Izumi Mitsuki.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.040
Yotsuba Tamaki.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.250
I'm Osaka Sogo.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.750
Hello. I'm Rokuya Nagi.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.250
I'm Nanase Riku.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.430
We're not debuting as seven?

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.180
Excuse me—

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.180
Roger that.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:39.970
I'm out.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.980
Please, at least participate 
in the audition!

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.060
I want to see more.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.150
I want to see you sing and dance.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.740
We pass?

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.970
All of us?

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.020
Yes!

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.170
Seriously?

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:57.640
Yes!

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.740
Fantastic! Amazing!

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.740
All right!

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.750
It'll be great working together, members!

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.340
"Don't look back

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.770
There's no time to look around

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.900
We found this Chance

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:14.760
We can't..." Huh?

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.800
It was moving.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.300
You're our role model.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.240
You can't beat me at dancing.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.850
What are you competing for?

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.430
We're promoting a concert!

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.690
Please take one.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.920
Take one.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.070
This is all because I was naive.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.370
We thought this might happen.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.820
Three thousand's too many off the bat.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.880
How many came? One? Two?

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.160
Huh? Uh, nine...

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:52.290
Okay. Let's throw a dance party 
with our nine guests tonight.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:57.170
Manager, thanks for working so hard 
to prepare for our first concert.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:02.050
We'll just fill the stands 
next time we perform here.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:09.890
For better or for worse, our beginning 
exists only in this moment today.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.900
Let's give everything we've got right now.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.080
Let's go!

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.410
Yeah!

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.500
Nice to meet you.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.920
We are...

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.190
IDOLiSH7!

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.830
I have to relearn everything from scratch.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:44.600
Come in!

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.270
Excuse me.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.790
Iori-san.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.980
Manager, I wanted to talk 
to you about the concert.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.900
I heard you directed everything 
related to tonight's concert.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.320
Yes. I'm sorry for the trouble I—

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:02.320
That's not why I ask.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.160
It was fantastic.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.030
Huh?

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.080
You're surprisingly talented.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.200
Excuse me?

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.810
The venue was too large this time.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:14.570
We've only just started to 
get our name out there,

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.240
but it wasn't bad.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.090
I see.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:20.470
Perhaps it's taboo for me 
to say this as an idol,

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.230
but why not let me,

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.570
the so-called perfect high school 
student, help you manage IDOLiSH7?

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.980
Their Feelings

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.410
It's huge.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.750
I heard it was pretty old.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.750
It's not at all, though.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.960
I want a corner room.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.800
This will be my bedroom.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.000
This will be my living room, and—

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.220
One room per person!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.180
Oh?

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.900
We'll be living here starting today.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:10.680
Yes. Starting today, this is your dorm.

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.610
Put that up in your own room!

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:34.580
No!

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.810
Iori-san, Tamaki-san.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:41.420
Did you get signatures from your guardians?

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.720
<b>Guardian Consent Form</b>

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.170
Here.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:45.720
Here's mine, too.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.510
Thank you.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.010
Oh, my guardian's name?

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:53.560
That's the director.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:55.350
Director?

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.020
I grew up in an orphanage.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.630
Didn't I tell you?

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.610
You're young, but your life hasn't been easy.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:03.360
Yeah.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.610
Sorry for eating your pudding the other day.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.800
I can't forgive you for that.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.370
S-Sorry...

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.380
Manager.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:12.290
Yes?

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.700
Do you have some time after this?

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:16.000
Yes.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.400
Is the manager okay?

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.720
Iori likes to lecture people.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.720
I seem to annoy him in particular.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.190
Oh, no.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:37.900
If anything, you and the manager are 
the type of people he loves to take care of.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.900
<b>IDOLiSH7 Planning
 Document (Draft)</b>

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.910
First, take a look at this document.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.400
Th-This is...

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:51.280
A concrete two-year plan covering 
up to and after your debut.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.490
It's only a draft.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:57.410
It can be adjusted according to our concept.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.760
Concept?

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:02.710
There's something I'd like 
you to decide first.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.220
Our center.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:09.590
Manager!

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:10.710
Riku-san.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.310
The gas burners won't turn on.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.020
Are they broken?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.980
Did you turn on the gas?

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.560
Oh, right. The main tap.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:23.480
Why don't you look things up on 
your phone before asking people?

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:28.000
Y-You don't have to put it like that!

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.160
It's my first time living 
away from my parents.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.620
It's my first time, too.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.060
And the manager lives at home.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.750
Well, if you're ever in trouble, 
don't count on my help!

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:40.930
Excuse me!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.450
How cute.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:46.200
What?

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:51.840
Picking up where we left off, our course 
will change depending on our center.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.850
For example, if it's Yotsuba-san, 
we'll focus on dancing.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.770
If it's Rokuya-san, we'll 
center around visuals.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.390
If it's Nikaido-san, we'll 
emphasize expression.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.110
With Osaka-san, we'll be 
a well-rounded group.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.650
With my brother, we'll be energetic.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:12.070
And if I were the center, we'd be 
flawlessly unified, but perhaps too tame.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:16.700
Manager, what color describes 
the group you imagine?

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.380
I-I...

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:25.580
I imagine a group loved 
and supported by everyone

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.280
that inspires dreams and gives hope.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.630
That's the kind of idol 
group I want to create.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.800
In that case, there's only one answer.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:39.220
What?! You want me to be the center?

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:42.980
Good luck.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.610
Everyone thinks you're a good singer.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.400
Nice, Riku!

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.900
Congratulations, Riku.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:52.070
Riku-kun, you can do it.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:52.910
Good luck.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:04.540
I, Nanase Riku, center of IDOLiSH7, 
will work like my life depends on it!

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:15.140
Anyway, what do we do now?

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.410
Shaking your heart (Say!)

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.300
Shaking your beat (Shout!)

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:19.560
Racing through time

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.390
Jump! (High!) Jump! (High!)

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:28.810
This vivid GENERATiON with you

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.030
It's a street performance.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.810
Hey, you're right.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:30.400
Who is it?

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:32.600
(One, Two, Three, Four,
Five, Six, Seven, Jump!!!)

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:37.610
It's the beginning Don't look back

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:41.250
There's no time to look away

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.660
They're so cool.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.390
We found this Chance

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:48.360
We can't let it go

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.900
Once we start running it's Non stop!

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:56.300
Changing at dizzying speeds is our Vision...

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.490
That's the summary of the tour.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:04.520
Any questions?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.520
No.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:06.900
No.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.900
I'm good.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.040
Really?

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:14.180
As your manager, I'm proud 
to manage such smart boys.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.520
Oh, right.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.370
I have a message from the president.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:25.200
"Don't be satisfied with 
this level," and such.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.150
Anyway, keep up the good work.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:33.550
Don't be satisfied, huh?

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:36.230
He's as tough as ever.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.050
He doesn't need to tell us.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.230
Thank you!

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:49.710
Thank you!

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:50.730
Thank you!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.690
We are IDOLiSH7!

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.240
We hope you at least remember our name!

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:02.470
I'm starting to get used to 
these street performances.

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:04.230
Yeah.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.120
Thank you.

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:07.910
Thanks for the support.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.080
We're IDOLiSH7.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.390
I'm hungry...

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.350
Encore!

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:19.130
Sing another song!

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.010
They want an encore.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:25.130
Thank you. Thanks for your support.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:25.170
In that case, let's do it!

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.200
I see.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:29.960
I'm from a cold country as well.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:31.060
Hey, Nagi!

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:37.570
<b>Yakisoba</b>

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:37.570
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:43.580
Guys!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.460
<b>Idol Self-Awareness Meeting</b>

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.770
We're idols!

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:52.420
Especially you, Nagi and Tamaki!

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:57.050
You lack focus.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:01.220
You sleep in, you're always late, and 
sometimes you dance however you want.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.640
No!

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:11.160
It's time for <i>Magical Cocona</i>!

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:13.410
All true devotees must watch it live!

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:20.700
<b>When watching TV, turn on the lights
 and watch from a distance</b>

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:16.930
<i>Magical Cocona</i> starts now!

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:20.700
Make sure you turn on the lights 
and watch from a distance.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:21.470
All right!

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:22.780
That's too close!

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.420
Woo!

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:26.790
Cocona is so cute!

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.790
Aw, jeez.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.790
Yes!

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.480
Yamato-san, say something.

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:33.110
You're the leader.

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:36.210
I prefer a hands-off approach.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.430
We should really take things seriously.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:40.340
Things are going well, after all.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:43.130
Oh, I am serious.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.550
I take singing and dancing seriously.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:49.170
I'm sorry I forgot to eat breakfast, 
but I do what I have to do.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:51.440
What's wrong with that?

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:53.100
But...

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.840
There's no telling when 
our fans are watching.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.700
We need to do better.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:00.550
We should strive to do 
everything five minutes early

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.320
so we don't cause problems for our manager.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.240
So-chan, you're too strict.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.710
My job is to sing and dance in this group.

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:13.990
I'll do my job, but I don't want anyone 
scolding me about anything else.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.200
Scolding?

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.890
Yeah, scolding.

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:18.340
You're no fun.

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:24.530
Is So mad?

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.930
It's probably the first time.

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:29.180
I'm not mad.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:31.600
S-Sorry...

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:36.480
Tamaki-kun, look at Iori-kun.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.440
He's your age, but he has it together.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.700
Let's take a break from performing.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:41.610
What?

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.810
Is what the manager is saying.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:45.530
Huh?

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.200
What?!

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:52.710
I never said we should stop performing.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.750
Are you stupid?

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:55.790
Stu—?!

00:12:55.790 --> 00:13:01.130
Surely they don't want the youngest member 
of the group telling them what to do.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:08.790
The best thing to do in this situation is stop 
performing and seek external stimulation.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.970
External stimulation?

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.990
There's something I'd like you to get.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:17.890
Tickets to TRIGGER's Arena 
Tour concert in Tokyo.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.650
Until TRIGGER's concert...

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:25.650
We're not performing for a month?

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:28.030
Oh, are we going on vacation?

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:31.910
Our street performances were just 
starting to get on track, though.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:38.330
That's exactly why we should stop 
performing and seek external stimulation.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:41.500
That doesn't sound like you, Manager.

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:46.380
A-And no singing or dancing 
until the concert.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.200
What?

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:48.570
Even that?

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:50.800
That's all. You're dismissed.

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:55.810
Thank you.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:06.250
We're taking a break from 
performing before our debut, huh?

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:08.450
Tama, what are you going to do for a month?

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.450
Go to school.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:14.320
Oh, right. You go to school with Ichi, right?

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:15.580
Yeah.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:22.170
Hey, why would a free spirit 
like you want to become an idol?

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:24.690
I want to be on TV.

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:27.050
TV, huh?

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:30.370
It's not that great.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:31.550
How about you?

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.300
Huh?

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.930
Why did you become an idol?

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:37.930
For revenge.

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:38.930
What?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.240
Just kidding!

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:43.510
Are you making fun of me?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:48.790
A month, huh? That's a long time.

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:59.090
Coming, coming!

00:15:01.010 --> 00:15:03.170
Thank you so much!

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.390
Yeah!

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:06.730
A delivery?

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:10.520
Yes. It's the complete box set of 
the second season of <i>Magical Cocona</i>.

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:13.610
I'm going to watch all 
of it over our vacation!

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.180
<i>MagiCona</i>!

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:19.770
No, no!

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.340
Please return my figures!

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:24.110
My complete box set!

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:25.610
Shut up!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:30.780
I'm taking this and that 
and that to the dumpster!

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.340
Oh, Jesus!

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:38.090
My magical stick! No!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:44.630
Nagi, I know you're more than 
just a womanizing anime nerd.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:50.090
More than when you're with 
girls or watching anime,

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:54.170
when you're dancing with 
us, you smile the brightest.

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:55.140
Right?

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:56.640
Mitsuki...

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.900
I know because I've been watching you.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:10.940
Man, you sure are handsome up close.

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:16.990
Mitsuki, I have a confession.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.080
U-Uh, okay.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:23.120
I am... beautiful.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:27.130
Dumpster shot!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:27.920
No!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.800
Flying Cocona!

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:33.550
I was ready to listen, and all 
you wanted to do was brag?

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.310
I'm a beautiful man!

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:39.470
I've had girlfriends, but never boyfriends!

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:43.670
You're all my first.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.750
Your first friends?

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:47.400
Yes.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:50.820
Oh. Why didn't you say so?

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:55.530
I did, but your dumpster shot...

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:58.940
Oh, right. Sorry about that.

00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:02.620
But, if we're friends, you 
shouldn't cause trouble for us.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.610
Sorry, my best friends.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:10.260
I thought everyone would be 
happy if I did what I liked.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:14.100
How do you have to be raised 
to end up thinking like that?

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:15.300
Sorry.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.590
Anyway, I'm surprised by that 
self-reflection from you.

00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:21.770
You can be kind of cute.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:27.310
I never even got the chance 
to scold my brother like this.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.310
Your brother Iori?

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:33.820
Yeah. I can never tell what he's thinking.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.100
Do you have a cold?

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:39.410
Don't worry. I take perfect 
care of my health.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:41.400
That's our schedule for the time being.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:42.790
Any questions?

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:45.590
No. Well, actually...

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:46.710
Go ahead.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:50.460
Iori-san, why did you want to become an idol?

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:53.940
Because it was my brother's dream.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.380
Mitsuki-san?

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:59.380
He met Zero and wished to become an idol.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.470
But he's small.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:05.860
He's not particularly good at 
singing or dancing, either.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:10.240
As he was going to every audition he could 
and getting rejected from every one,

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:11.900
I was scouted.

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:16.530
So I told the president I'd do it
 if my brother could join me.

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:20.230
My brother has the power to 
energize the people around him,

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:24.390
though ordinary people
 tend to overlook that.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.760
Brothers can be so strange.

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:29.250
You think so?

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:32.840
Come to think of it, I heard 
Riku-san has an older brother, too.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.870
I'm sure he does.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:38.130
He's your typical spoiled younger brother.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.090
Younger brother?

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.470
You mean like you?

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:43.990
Yes.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.140
So you should...

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:48.890
Spoil me sometimes.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.480
Excuse me.

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.650
G-Good work!

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:02.500
Good morning.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.810
Riku-kun, are you up first today?

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.320
Good morning.

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.170
Iori, good morning.

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:09.410
Good morning.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:11.250
Want some coffee?

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.380
Sure.

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:13.600
Where are the others?

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:14.970
Still asleep.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:21.380
The anime viewing Rokuya-san held 
last night went until the morning.

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:23.390
Magical Flash!

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:25.270
Magical Flash!

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:25.270
Yeah!

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:28.890
Oh, right. They were really into it.

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:34.390
Since we're forbidden 
from singing and dancing,

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:36.970
I don't know what to do with my free time.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:38.150
Here.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.480
Thank you.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.740
Thanks.

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:44.450
We need to wake Tamaki or he'll be late!

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.290
Tamaki! Get up!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.160
You're going to be late!

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:59.260
I told you to set an alarm.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:02.370
Don't fall asleep on your way to school.

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:05.730
We're off.

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:08.140
See you later.

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:13.100
What should we do today?

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:20.360
I feel like I haven't been here in forever.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:25.830
The lesson room feels sad 
when we can't sing or dance.

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:27.170
Yeah.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.870
There's still 20 more days 
until the TRIGGER concert.

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:40.520
Sogo-san...

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:45.930
Sogo-san, what do you think of TRIGGER?

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.590
I like them.

00:20:47.590 --> 00:20:49.920
Their singing and dancing has intensity.

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:52.040
I'm looking forward to their concert.

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:55.850
I can lend you their albums sometime if—

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:55.850
I...

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.110
I'm not so sure.

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:00.260
Huh?

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:04.930
I don't know if I like TRIGGER or not.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:08.470
If I can respect them or forgive them.

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:09.530
Riku-kun?

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:15.120
Sogo-san, why did you 
decide to become an idol?

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:19.980
For example, do you think you'd be able to...

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:23.480
abandon your family for 
the sake of your dream?

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:28.760
Oh, sorry. That was a weird thing to ask.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:30.410
I already have.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:31.100
Huh?

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:34.070
You can't be serious.

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:38.770
But someone as kind as you could 
never do something so cruel.

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:40.210
It's true.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.700
Sorry, I probably let you down.

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:46.090
I should go.

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:47.110
Sogo-san!

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:03.850
Why?

00:22:27.690 --> 00:22:34.100
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:22:34.100 --> 00:22:37.800
Someday we'll make it past there

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:43.400
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:50.370
We don't know what's right

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:53.560
So we Try and Jump!

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:56.720
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:22:56.720 --> 00:23:00.120
For us It's Only Way!

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:03.470
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:23:03.470 --> 00:23:07.000
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:09.490
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:10.590
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:11.320
Live! (Yeah!)

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:15.030
In the light!

00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:15.740
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:22.090
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:25.040
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:28.560
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:35.050
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:41.700
The future surely lies on the other side

00:23:41.700 --> 00:23:45.060
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:48.130
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:23:48.130 --> 00:23:54.120
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!
